$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Cu-Catalyzed
β-Borylation of Thioacetylenes. To a mixture of CuCl (5.0 mg, 0.05 mmol),
DPEphos (27.0 mg, 0.05 mmol), NaOt-Bu (7.2 mg, 0.075 mmol), and B2pin2
(2a) (69.9 mg, 0.55 mmol) was added a solution of 1a (81 mg, 0.5 mmol) in
2 mL of MeOH under a nitrogen atmosphere. After stirring at 35 °C for 12
h, the reaction mixture was concentrated and purified by column
chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1) on silica gel to give 3a.
Compound 3d. 83% yield (135 mg); white solid. mp: 90-92 °C, β/α = 92:8;
Rf = 0.27 (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 1.25
(s, 12H), 1.30 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3H), 2.76 (q, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 7.16-7.29
(m, 3H), 7.31 (s, 1H), 7.35-7.39 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ
15.4, 24.6, 28.1, 83.4, 126.4, 128.0, 129.3, 130.2, 132.6, 138.7, 146.2;
MS (EI, m/z): 326 (2), 324 (M+, 6), 289 (54), 263 (2), 197 (12); HRMS
(EI) calcd for C16H22BClO2S (M+) 324.1122, found 324.1120.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
