$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Experimental Procedure for NHC-Cu-Catalyzed Hydroboration of Allene 6e
with Bis(pinacolato)diboron: In an N2 filled glove box, an oven-dried 1
dram vial equipped with a stir bar was charged with SIMes (2.4 mg, 7
μmol), CuCl (0.6 mg, 6.4 μmol), NaOt-Bu (3.7 mg, 39 μmol) and thf (2.2
mL). The mixture was sealed with a cap (phenolic open top cap with red
PTFE/white silicone septum) and allowed to stir for 30 min at 22 °C.
Bis(pinacolato)diboron (36.0 mg, 0.142 mmol) was added to the solution,
causing it to turn dark brown immediately. The vial was re-sealed with a
cap (phenolic open top cap with red PTFE/white silicone septum) and
removed from the glove box. The mixture was allowed to stir at 22 °C for
30 min under an atmosphere of N2. A solution of allene 6e (24.0 mg, 0.129
mmol) in thf (0.4 mL) and MeOH (7.6 μL, 0.193 mmol) were added through a
micro-syringe. The reaction was allowed to stir at 22 °C for 6 h, and
then it was quenched by passing through a short plug of silica gel (4 cm
x 1 cm) and eluted with Et2O. The organic layer was concentrated under
reduced pressure, resulting in a yellow oil which was purified by silica
gel chromatography (1:70 Et2O:hexanes, Rf 0.17) to afford the
un-separable mixture of 17 and 18 (17:18=9:1).
(S)-4-(2-Methoxyphenyl)-2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1,5-hexadiene
(17), clear oil, yield 34.1 mg, 0.107 mmol, 84%; 18, yield 84%. (17): IR
(neat): 3064 (w), 2977 (m), 2934 (m), 2835 (w), 1635 (w), 1617 (w), 1598
(w), 1585 (w), 1491 (s), 1463 (m), 1437 (m), 1366 (s), 1306 (s), 1239
(s), 1212 (m), 1164 (m), 1139 (s), 1107 (m), 1052 (m), 1030 (s), 995 (w),
970 (m), 939 (m), 910 (m), 861 (s), 832 (w), 808 (w), 783 (w), 750 (s),
671 (s), 578 (m), 517 (w), 485 (w) cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ
7.17-7.12 (2H, m), 6.89 (1H, dd, J = 7.6, 1.2 Hz), 6.83 (1H, d, J = 7.6
Hz), 6.06-5.97 (1H, m), 5.73 (1H, d, J = 3.6 Hz), 5.49 (1H, d, J = 3.6
Hz), 4.98-4.95 (2H, m), 3.98 (1H, ddd, J = 7.6, 7.6, 7.6 Hz), 3.80 (3H,
s), 2.55 (2H, dd, J = 13.2, 7.6 Hz), 1.25 (12H, s); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100
MHz): δ 156.9, 141.6, 132.5, 130.4, 128.1, 126.8, 120.4, 113.9, 110.7,
83.2, 55.3, 42.3, 40.0, 30.8, 24.7; HRMS (ESI+): Calcd for C19H28B1O3
[M+H]+: 315.2131; Found: 315.2129; specific rotation: [α ]D 24.6 +5.5 (c
= 1.70, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, glovebox used, sealed vial used, 96:4 er, mechanism
studied
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Site- and Enantioselective Formation of Allene-Bearing Tertiary or
Quaternary Carbon Stereogenic Centers through NHC-Cu-Catalyzed Allylic
Substitution
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jung, Byunghyuck; Hoveyda, Amir H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2012), 134(3), 1490-1493

