$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the regioselective
borylation of internal alkynes. Synthesis of
(Z)-2-((3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)but-2-en-1-yl)sulfonyl)pyridine
(5) A screw-capped vial was charged withCuCl (2.6 mg, 0.026 mmol, 10
mol%), NaOtBu (3.8 mg, 0.039 mmol, 15 mol%), bis(pinacolato)diboron (73.2
mg, 0.288 mmol, 1.1 equiv), tricyclohexylphosphine (9 mg, 0.0314 mmol, 12
mol%) and 2-(but-2-yn-1-ylsulfonyl)pyridine (II) (51.2 mg, 0.262 mmol)
and the vial was purged and backfilled with argon (3 times).To this
mixture were added toluene (0.7 mL) and MeOH (22 μL, 0.524 mmol) and the
resulting solution was stirred at room temperature until no starting
material was detected (TLC monitoring, the specific time is given for
each substrate). Then, the reaction was quenched with MeOH, filtered
through a pad of Celite (washed with DCM) and the filtrate concentrated
to dryness. The obtained crude was purified by flash chromatography (40%
EtOAc/hexanes) to obtain 5 .
(Z)-4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(4-(phenylthio)but-2-en-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(2) Reaction time: 2h. Chromatography: 20% EtOAc in hexanes. Colorless
oil, yield: 57.8 mg (76%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCL3)δ = 7.38 -7.31 (m, 2
H), 7.30 -7.23 (m, 4 H), 7.22 -7.13 (m, 1 H), 6.40 (qt, J = 1.8, 7.5 Hz,
1 H), 3.63 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2 H), 1.66 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 3 H), 1.25 (s, 12
H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCL3)δ = 139.5, 131.6, 129.7, 128.8, 126.1, 83.4,
32.0, 24.8, 13.8.11B NMR (160 MHz, CDCL3) δ = 29.8 HRMS-ESI
(m/z):Calculated for [C16H23BO2S+H]: 291.1584, found: 291.1581.
