$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A schlenk tube equipped with a magnetic
stirring bar was charged with (IMes)AgCl (6.0 μmol), potassium
tert-butoxide (1 M solution in THF, 0.018 mmol), an alkyne (0.45 mmol),
bis(pinacolato)diboron (0.30 mmol) and MeOH (1.0 mL). The mixture was
stirred at 50 °C for the period as specified in Table 2 and Scheme 1, and
diluted with ethyl acetate before filtration through a Celite plug. The
organic solution was washed twice with brine and dried over MgSO4.
Evaporation of the solvent followed by silica gecolumm chromatoghy
(hexane/dichloromethane as an eluent) or gel permeation chromatography
(chloroform as an eluent) gave the corresponding product. In 13C NMR
spectra, boron-bound carbons were not detected because of quadrupolar
relaxation.
(Z)-2-(1-Cyclohexylprop-1-en-2-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolane
((Z)-4b) Isolated in 85% as a pale yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.04-1.33
(m, 17H), 1.60-1.73 (m, 5H), 1.68 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 3H), 2.35 (dtt, J =
8.9, 3.7, 11.0 Hz, 1H), 6.12 (dq, J = 8.8, 1.7 Hz, 1H) 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
13.89, 24.79, 25.95, 26.08, 32.20, 37.49, 83.02, 151.81 All the
resonances in 1H and 13C spectra were consistent with reported values.14
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
